From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:25:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: cap TDLib's log verbosity at 1

TDLib logs at verbosity 5 unless told otherwise, which writes out every
network query and update. On webOS the plugin runs inside the shared IM
transport, whose output ends up in one log (/media/internal/imstdout.log)
with every other plugin's, and TDLib alone filled it at about 1.5 MB a
minute, burying everything else.

Set the verbosity to 1 (fatal errors and warnings) right before each client
is created. This overrides the level tgprpl_init() derives from libpurple's
debug settings.

Not for upstream: elsewhere that derived level is the right control.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 transceiver.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/transceiver.cpp b/transceiver.cpp
index 73aeb69..bdfc054 100644
--- a/transceiver.cpp
+++ b/transceiver.cpp
@@ -49,8 +49,14 @@ TdTransceiverImpl::TdTransceiverImpl(PurpleTdClient *owner, TdTransceiver::Updat
     m_updateCb(updateCb),
     m_lastQueryId(0)
 {
-    if (!testBackend)
+    if (!testBackend) {
+        // webOS: tdlib defaults to verbosity 5 (logs every network query + update), which floods
+        // the shared transport log (/media/internal/imstdout.log) at ~1.5MB/min and buries every
+        // other plugin's output. Cap it to 1 (fatal errors + warnings only) before creating the
+        // client. Static execute() applies process-wide to tdlib's native logger.
+        td::Client::execute({0, td::td_api::make_object<td::td_api::setLogVerbosityLevel>(1)});
         m_client = std::make_unique<td::Client>();
+    }
 }
 
 TdTransceiverImpl::~TdTransceiverImpl()
